# TypeScript

Prefer `interface` for object shapes, prefixed with `I` when the shape is a new public contract (`IOrderFormProps`). Domain models that already live in `@saf-shekan/core` keep their existing names (`OrderConfig`, `SniperState`, `BotConfig`) — do not rename them.

Use `type` for unions and aliases (`SniperState`, `BrokerType`).

Never `any` or `as any`. Use `unknown` and narrow, or Zod parse.

Shared order, timing, broker, and fee types belong in `@saf-shekan/core`. Feature-local props stay next to the component.

Nest DTOs mirror core interfaces. Do not duplicate a second order model in the frontend.
